CableCreation DP to DVI male-to-male cable connects DisplayPort equipped computer to a DVI monitor/ HDTV/ projector for video streaming, ideal for video streaming, gaming, or extending a workstation. It also supports DP, DP++ and DisplayPort++. 
Specification: 
Output Side: DisplayPort male;
Input Side: DVI male;
Support resolution up to 1920*1200 / 1080P@60Hz Full HD;
Plug and play, no driver or software is needed.
Warm Tips: 
The Display to DVI cable is NOT bi-directional, it can only transfer signal from the Displayport source device to a DVI monitor/ HDTV/ projector.

Foil & braid shielding reduces unnecessary interference and provides stable signal transmission;
Tinned copper conductor improves cable performance;
PVC jacket ensures cable flexibility.

Works for devices with a Toslink (S/PDIF or Optical) port, like: 
Sound bars (Vizio, Sony, Samsung, LG, Bose, Sharp, Philips, Polk, Yamaha); 
TV (Vizio, Samsung, Apple, LG, Sharp, Sony); 
Game consoles / PlayStations (PS3, PS4, Xbox One, Xbox One S, XBox 360, Sony PlayStation); 
CD / DVD / Blu-Ray players; 
Home / Audio theater receivers; 
Preamplifiers; 
Digital satellites; 
Audio processors; 
Digital-to-analog converters (DACs).
